# Build outputs
bin/
obj/
build/

# Replays written by --outdir
solutions/
solutions_*/
archive_runs/

# Per-session run campaigns (sessions 4-5: mA_*..mO_*, sA_*..sY_*;
# sessions 6-7: sZ6_*, s7_*)
m[A-Z]*_*/
s[0-9A-Z]*_*/

# Release packaging (tools/build_release.ps1)
dist/
combosolver-*.zip

# Logs and working files
*.log

__pycache__/

# --- measurement harnesses ---
# One file per A/B or battery that was run once, and from which a figure quoted
# in docs/ came. They are the executable record of a measurement, not tools:
# every one of them hard-codes this machine's paths, most hard-code a seed and a
# budget, and a third depend on an output directory produced by an earlier
# session. They stay on disk as an archive and out of the repository, so that
# tools/ holds only what actually builds or inspects the project.
measurements/

# --- WebAssembly port ---
# It no longer lives here: its sources are on the `web` branch, together with
# the browser workshop and the documents that only make sense for that page.
# What is left in wasm/ on this branch is a BUILD tree (91 MB of module, packed
# data and node_modules) that we want neither to track nor to delete: ignored
# wholesale.
wasm/

# --- working notes ---
# Session reports, states of the art and design notes: the record of how the
# solver got here, written for one reader. They stay on disk and out of the
# repository, which carries what builds and what runs.
docs/

# --- replay templates ---
# build_release.ps1 trains the PGO profile on the file passed as -Gabarit, so
# the training input is supplied per machine instead of being tracked.
gabarits/

# --- verification scripts ---
# sympy proofs, LP duals, closed forms, replay inspection: each verified one
# result once and is quoted in docs/. Same rule as measurements/ above. tools/
# keeps only the two scripts that fetch the dependencies and build the release.
tools/*.py
